    pr_ref:  # 170c
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-03 while designing WI-suhug's write-side seam, on dev de3538531b, by asking the shipped derivation what an UNSTAMPED gated call mints.\n\nSTATEMENT. For a primitive declared under two or more boundaries of one direction and narrowed by `io_target_kind` (INV-zumin class (b)), a call whose stamp ABSTAINS -- absent, an unknown kind, or collapsed sites that disagree -- must derive the same taint entry that `classify_call` selects for it: the `abstains_to` row (INV-fatok), else the first declared row. The two consumers read one catalogue and must give one answer.\n\nVIOLATION, measured with the production derivation and matcher (`_derive_auto_imports_from_io_primitives` + `_build_callee_index` + `_match_propagation_entry`):\n  go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved   unstamped   classify -> ipc_recv (abstains_to)   taint SOURCE -> None\n  go:bufio:0-0:NewReader:unresolved    unstamped   classify -> ipc_recv                 taint SOURCE -> None\n  go:bufio:0-0:NewScanner:unresolved   std_stream  classify -> ipc_recv                 taint SOURCE -> untrusted_input (correct)\nOn the six-repo WI-vutav corpus 19 constructor sites are unstamped (2 alertmanager, 2 beads, 4 caddy, 11 cilium) and every one mints nothing. Two of them are `cluster/tls_connection.go:136` (alertmanager) and `httpredirectlistener.go:91` (caddy) -- the exact sites INV-bagok's go.yaml note names as the reason the fallback is ipc_recv: \"Each would lose a TRUE untrusted_input source.\" They were lost anyway, one consumer over.\n\nROOT CAUSE. The derivation marks every SOURCE of a target-kind-gated primitive `requires_target_kind=<its boundary>` (WI-lipis, correct: the ipc_recv source must not fire by name at a file read), and `_match_propagation_entry` admits a gated entry only when `resolve_target_kind_across_sites` returns exactly that boundary. `None` from the resolver is documented there as \"an abstention ... deliberately admits only the unconditional entries\". For c's `fgets` (fallback fs_read, which mints nothing) that equals the classifier's answer by luck of AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP; for a primitive whose fallback row MINTS it silently deletes the source. INV-bagok's dual row turned bufio's unconditional source into a gated one on the day it landed, and nothing asked the taint side what the fallback now was. `_apply_abstention_targets` and the INV-fatok arm in `classify_call` carry the fallback; the taint index never learned it.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS MORE ON THE WRITE SIDE. Sinks are untouched today only because no write primitive is target-kind-gated -- `_target_kind_discriminated_keys` is \"two or more READ boundaries\". WI-suhug generalises that rule; without a fallback clause every unstamped `io.WriteString` and `fmt.Fprintf` would lose its sink -- a false-all-clear -- and the same would happen to c/cpp `unistd.write` and haskell `hPutStr*`, which become gated by the same generalisation.\n\nFIX (one mechanism for both entry kinds, shipped with WI-suhug): the derivation records, per gated primitive, which row is the fallback (the first row after `_apply_abstention_targets`, which is exactly what the classifier selects) and marks that row's entry `abstention_fallback`; the matcher admits an entry when it is unconditional, when the stamp resolves to its boundary, or when the stamp abstains and the entry is the fallback. `TaintSink` gains `requires_target_kind` alongside `requires_mode`. Behavioural closure evidence required: the repro above re-run (unstamped NewScanner mints), c `write` / haskell `hPutStr` / go `io.WriteString` unstamped sinks unchanged, and every read-side source the fix adds on the six repos read back individually."  # 170c
    fields:  # 170c
      statement: "For a primitive declared under two or more boundaries of one direction and narrowed by io_target_kind, a call whose stamp abstains (absent, unknown kind, or disagreeing collapsed sites) derives the same taint entry that classify_call selects for it: the abstains_to row, else the first declared row. One catalogue, one answer."  # 170c
      root_cause: "The taint derivation marks every entry of a target-kind-gated primitive requires_target_kind=<its boundary> and _match_propagation_entry admits a gated entry only when the stamp resolves to exactly that boundary; None from the resolver admits only unconditional entries, so an abstention drops the whole primitive. _apply_abstention_targets and the INV-fatok arm in classify_call carry the fallback; the taint index never learned it. Equal to the classifier only when the fallback row mints nothing (c fgets), by luck of AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP."  # 170c
